<article class="env-lemma" id="0G25">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G25">Lemma <span data-tag="0G25">57.11.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ and $Y$ be proper schemes over $k$. Assume $X$ is regular. Then a $k$-linear exact functor $F : D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ is fully faithful if and only if for any closed points $x, x' \in X$ the maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F : \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_ X(\mathcal{O}_ x, \mathcal{O}_{x'}) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_ Y(F(\mathcal{O}_ x), F(\mathcal{O}_{x'}))  \]
</div>
  <p> are isomorphisms for all $i \in \mathbf{Z}$. Here $\mathcal{O}_ x$ is the skyscraper sheaf at $x$ with value $\kappa (x)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0FYN" data-tag="0FYN">57.7.1</a> the functor $F$ has both a left and a right adjoint. Thus we may apply the criterion of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G24" data-tag="0G24">57.11.1</a> because assumptions (2) and (3) of that lemma follow from Lemma <a href="/tag/0G03" data-tag="0G03">57.11.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>